Hi Fabio

    To install SSH you need to make a download of  file=20
ftp://ftp.unicamp.br/pub/security/tools/ssh/ssh-3.2.3.tar.gz  to=20
/usr/local/security (suggestion). After this, run the commands:
    1 ) cd /usr/local/security
    2 ) gzip -dc ssh-3.2.3.tar.gz | tar xvf -
    3 ) cd ssh-3.2.3
    4 ) ./config     (verify the compilers that you have, and set the=20
parameters)
    5 ) make
    6 ) make install

    Sometimes you need create a new entry um /sbin/rc3.d to start SSH=20
daemon in boot sequence.
    Good luck. :-)



