13 quick replies and even a script from Alan Davis.  Below is Johan
Brusche's reply:

cd /dev
/MAKEDEV tzN       <<<--- where N=(scsi-bus-nbr*8+tape-target-nmbr)
				eg tz5 if drive is on bus #0 target#5
                     use "/sbin/scu sho edt" if you do not know the numbers.

I didn't get to try the scu command in the environment of being booted off
of cdrom exit to O/S shell.  Turns out the device was tz0.  I figure it's  a
good idea to have a printed copy of "uerf -R -r 300" around.

