Nothing was done in V5.x to block support on the AlphaServer 800, and
if the AlphaServer 3000 (which was NEVER supported in Digital UNIX or
DEC OSF/1 or Tru64 UNIX because it was sold only to run Windows NT)
is really essentially the same hardware as an AlphaServer 800 AND you
can get an SRM console running on it that really makes it look to the
OS as an AlphaServer 800, then it would probably just work (although
it may have hardware options that will not work, including maybe the
boot device, etc.)

What WAS decommisioned in V5.1A and later was the DEC 3000 and other
old machines that didn't have PCI bus support. 

